  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In September 2024 testimony, Helena Fu said DOE has infrastructure to support frontier-scale AI development and that the United States must lead in advanced AI for scientific, energy, and national security applications. In December 2023 testimony, she said rapid AI development carries unprecedented risks and that protecting rights and safety requires evaluating and mitigating AI-related risks. In 2024 testimony, she described DOE’s FASST initiative as a national AI capability intended to provide frontier-scale AI systems and support AI governance and safety measures.",
   "sids": [
